-- =============================================================================
-- 0006 — Nineteen ways the work actually goes
--
-- The library has thousands of tasks and nothing saying what order they happen
-- in. A concrete estimate could name every step and could not say that the
-- forms go up before the pour — which is the difference between a price and a
-- schedule.
--
-- These are nineteen ordered sequences: concrete, demolition, electrical,
-- excavation, HVAC, openings, plumbing fixtures, plumbing lines, pressure
-- washing, residential remodel, DOT, maintenance of traffic, finishes, project
-- controls, specialty systems, and four drone missions — mapping, inspection,
-- thermal and media.
--
-- **40 rows were dropped, and that is the important part.** The file held two
-- generations of the same sequences, merged and never reconciled: an older
-- four-step version and a current ten-step one, sharing step numbers 1 to 4.
-- Ten of the nineteen templates were affected. Imported as they arrived, a
-- concrete estimate would have carried "Layout" twice and treated "Form /
-- reinforce" and "Set forms / edges" as different work.
--
-- The two are cleanly separable: every superseded row has a blank
-- `trade_family` and every current one has it filled. Dropping the 40 leaves
-- all nineteen templates with an unbroken 1..n sequence, which was checked
-- rather than assumed.
--
-- **The production rates are the ones actually stated** — 19 of them, and nothing
-- is invented for the rest. 80 CY/HR to excavate and 95 to haul are numbers
-- somebody put there; a step with no rate carries none rather than a
-- placeholder that would score as knowledge.
--
-- `MISSION` became `EA`: a drone mission is one thing, flown once. `AC` became
-- `ACRE`, the same measurement under a shorter name.
-- =============================================================================

insert into library_categories (company_id, kind, name, sort_order)
select null, 'crew_discipline', v.name, v.sort
from (values ('Project Controls', 600), ('Pressure Washing', 610),
             ('Maintenance of Traffic', 620), ('Transportation', 630),
             ('Windows / Doors', 640), ('Residential Remodel', 650),
             ('Specialty', 660), ('Drone', 670), ('Demolition', 680),
             ('Excavation', 690), ('General', 700)
) as v(name, sort)
on conflict do nothing;

